# Cell from playpick: mode=menus, view=1280x800, save=carried.
#
# First menus session on a non-touch (mouse, desktop) viewport -- the four
# prior menus sessions (2026-09-25-9, -19, -30, 2026-09-26-1/-2) were all
# 820x1180,touch. First use of `key escape` anywhere in this job's history
# (grepped playtest/plans/ -- no prior script has ever sent it).
#
# The thing worth testing: input.ts sets `menuRequested = true` on any
# Escape/P keydown regardless of what screen is showing (the listener is
# global, attached to `window`), but `takeMenuRequest()` -- the only place
# that ever reads and clears that flag -- is called from exactly one call
# site, inside the fight screen's own update function (src/main.ts:2283,
# "leaving mid-fight is always available"). No menu screen (settings,
# citadel, composition, record) ever calls it. So: press Escape while on a
# plain menu screen, confirm nothing visibly happens there (expected, since
# nothing reads the flag on that screen), then walk into a fresh pull and
# see whether the *next* fight silently eats the stale request and bounces
# to the roster before the player has done anything in it -- a "menu key
# with no effect where you pressed it, and an effect where you didn't
# expect one" bug, if it reproduces.

open
targets
shot front

tap settings
targets
shot settings-before-escape
key Escape
wait 1
targets
shot settings-after-escape
state

tap back
tap raid
tap next
targets
tap class:mage:frost
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
targets
state
shot fight-immediately

# Stuck on roster with mode already travel -- does a second PULL recover it,
# or is the evening wedged the way THE VIGIL's wipe is in #271?
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
targets
state
shot fight-second-attempt

